  2. File management commands
  *****************************************************
  Command         	Purpose
cat file.txt	    Display file content
less file.txt   	Read large files
head file.txt	    Show first 10 lines
tail file.txt	    Show last 10 lines
tail -f app.log	  Monitor live logs
grep "error" app.log	      Search errors
grep -i "failed" app.log	   Search ignoring case
wc -l file.txt	              Count lines
sort file.txt                	Sort lines
uniq file.txt	                    Remove adjacent duplicates
cut -d: -f1 /etc/passwd	          Extract usernames

 grep -i "error" /var/log/syslog   -> Check application errors
 tail -f /var/log/syslog ->Monitor live logs

